  "seoBody": "<h2>Pay for reports, not seats</h2><p>Quickler pricing is one pound per completed report. Pick the monthly bundle that suits your team. Unlimited users, unlimited managers, unlimited workflows on every plan &mdash; you only pay for the reports you finish. UK customers can pay by UK Direct Debit; card is available everywhere.</p><h2>What is included</h2><ul><li><strong>Unlimited users.</strong> Add every engineer, manager and admin in your firm at no extra cost.</li><li><strong>Unlimited workflows.</strong> Run EICR, CP12, van checks, site reports and any custom inspection on the same plan.</li><li><strong>Human sign-off.</strong> The accountable person reviews and edits every draft before it is finalised.</li><li><strong>Evidence kept with the job.</strong> Photos, voice notes and measurements stay attached to the record they belong to.</li><li><strong>PDF export.</strong> Finished reports are produced ready to send, file or store.</li><li><strong>No setup fee.</strong> Standard plans have no onboarding charge.</li></ul><h2>Why per report and not per engineer</h2><p>Most inspection software charges per seat, which punishes you for adding staff. Quickler charges for finished work instead, so a firm with twenty occasional users pays the same as one with five heavy users on the same report volume. Here is the full reasoning on <a href=\"/pages/no-subscription-compliance.html\">per-report versus per-engineer pricing</a>.</p><h2>Bigger volumes and other countries</h2><p>Need more than 500 reports a month? The same pound-per-report rate applies, billed to suit your volume &mdash; <a href=\"mailto:hello@quickler.co\">talk to us</a>. Rooted in UK compliance, <a href=\"/pages/global-field-compliance.html\">Quickler works in any country</a> WhatsApp does, across English-speaking markets including the UK, Ireland, the United States, Canada, Australia and New Zealand.</p>",
